 & Events\nUpcoming Events\nNews\nPast News & Events\nMedia Coverage\nFeature Stories\nMedia Contact\nAlumni & Friends\nAlumni Stories\nReunions & Homecomings\nGiving\nWays to Give\nH.K.U.E.A.A.\nContact Update Form\nAdmission Requirements\nAdmissions PhD/MPhil Admission Requirements\nContent\nAdmission Requirements\nThe basic qualification necessary for admission to research postgraduate studies is a good honours degree from this University or an equivalent qualification from a comparable institution. A summary of basic admission requirements is listed as follows:\nAdmission Requirements\nMaster of Philosophy (MPhil)\nBachelor's degree with Second Class Honours Division I or above; or\nBachelor's degree with Second Class Honours Division II and a taught Master's degree\n4-year Doctor of Philosophy (4-year PhD)\nBachelor\u2019s degree with First Class Honours preferably with research experience; or\nBachelor\u2019s degree with Second Class Honours Division I and a taught Master\u2019s degree\n3-year Doctor of Philosophy (3-year PhD)\nBachelor\u2019s degree with Second Class Honours Division I or above and a research Master\u2019s degree (MPhil)\nCandidates will be selected based on, but not limited to, the following criteria:\nApplicant's academic qualifications\nQuality of research proposal\nResearch experience/track record/publications\nComments made by referees\nIn addition, certain degree courses have more specific requirements. Qualifying examinations to test the applicants\u2019 abilities to follow the prescribed courses and/or interviews may be conducted. Applicants with qualifications other than an honours degree are considered on their individual merits.\nApplicants who wish to be admitted to higher degrees on the basis of a qualification from a university or a comparable institution outside Hong Kong where the language of teaching and/or examination is not English are required to obtain the following:\nan overall score of 85 or above (for tests taken before Jan 21, 2026) or an overall score of 4.5 or above (for tests taken from Jan 21, 2026 onwards) in the Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL); or\na minimum overall band of 6.5 with no subtest lower than 6 in the International English Language Testing System (IELTS) (Academic module); or\ngrade C or above in the Overseas General Certificate of Education (GCE); or\ngrade C or above in the International General Certificate of Secondary Education (IGCSE); or\ngrade C or above in the Cambridge Test of Proficiency in English Language (CPE).\nSince places for research postgraduate studies are limited, it may not be possible to offer admission to all qualified applicants. For more information, please read FAQ on Admission.\nAdmissions\nPhD/MPhil\nApplication Procedures\nAdmission Requirements\nProgramme Structure\nScholarships, Financial Assistance and Fees\nPostgraduate Admissions Advisors\nFAQ\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 by Faculty of Engineering, The University of Hong Kong\nContact Us |\nLinkedIn |\nFacebook |\nInstagram |\nYouTube |\nPrivacy Policy | Web Accessibility", "links": [["", "https://engg.hku.hk/"], ["Wellness@HKU", "https://wellness.hku.hk"], ["Student Support Centre", "https://engg.hku.hk/Students-Support-Centre"], ["HKU Home", "https://hku.hk/"], ["HKU Portal", "http://hkuportal.hku.hk"], ["", "https://engg.hku.hk/Admissions/PhD-MPhil/Admission-Requirements"], ["Search", "javascript:__doPostBack('dnn$dnnSEARCH$cmdSearch','')"], ["About Us", "https://engg.hku.hk/About-Us"], ["Message from the Dean", "https://engg.hku.hk/About-Us/Message-from-the-Dean"], ["Vision and Mission", "https://engg.hku.hk/About-Us/Vision-and-Mission"], ["History", "https://engg.hku.hk/About-Us/History"], ["List of Deans (1912-)", "https://engg.hku.hk/About-Us/History/List-of-Deans"], ["Dean's Office", "https://engg.hku.hk/About-Us/Deans-Office"], ["Academic Staff", "https://engg.hku.hk/About-Us/Academic-Staff"], ["Departments/Schools", "https://engg.hku.hk/About-Us/Departments"],